# Documentation for /usr/local/bin/folk-around

folk-around is an MCP (Model Context Protocol) daemon for computer control.
It speaks MCP over stdio, HTTP SSE, or Cloudflare signaling plus local HTTP. Written in Zig.

## Usage

    folk-around [options]

Options:
  --verbose      Show tool calls
  --mode <mode>  Security mode: full, limited, sandbox
  --http <port>  HTTP SSE transport mode (e.g. 8080)
  --p2p          Print pairing code, join saved/default signaling server, and start local HTTP
  --signal-server <url>  Custom signaling server URL
  --room <name>  Pairing code / signaling room name
  --help         This help

## Modes

full — unrestricted shell, full access
limited — read-only shell commands, no write
sandbox — no shell, a11y + file ops only

## Tools

folk_shell, folk_system_info, folk_list_apps, folk_spawn,
folk_clipboard_read, folk_clipboard_write, folk_osascript,
folk_tell, folk_screenshot

## Transports

stdio (default): MCP protocol over stdin/stdout. Pipe to any MCP client.
HTTP SSE: Use --http <port>. GET /sse for events, POST /message for calls.
Signaling: Use --p2p or --signal-server <url>. Prints a pairing code, joins /signal/<room>, and starts local HTTP MCP. The last server, code, port, and mode are saved under ~/.config/folk-around/config.

## Examples

  folk-around                                          # stdio mode, full access
  folk-around --mode sandbox                          # sandbox mode
  folk-around --http 8080                             # HTTP SSE on port 8080
  folk-around --signal-server folkaround.undivisible.dev
  echo '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"tools/list"}' | folk-around
